If you accept my definition of jbomass as something that encompasses
Collective, Substance, and Substance-derived-from-Collective, then
it is quite possible that CLL Lojban has something that means
Collective but is (accurately) labelled by the more inclusive term
'jbomass'. {mei} seems such a thing. {pa lo re mei} is a countable
collective, a single pair. {loi su'o mei} is a jbomass of collective,
one or more collectives treated as Substance.

If it were possible to kill the piQ before lei, then leiza'u would
probably give you an uncountable collective ("*People* crowded the
streets. They clamoured for justice."). I don't know of any way of 
killing the piQ, though. I can't think how to get a nonspecific 
uncountable collective -- all ideas I have had turned out to fail.

